  "prompt": "Postgres: JSON_OBJECTAGG with a key/value pair is written as invalid JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v)\n\nA `JSON_OBJECTAGG` with a key/value pair is written for Postgres as `JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v)`, which is invalid there.\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import transpile\ntranspile(\"SELECT JSON_OBJECTAGG(k VALUE v) FROM t\", read=\"postgres\", write=\"postgres\")\ntranspile(\"SELECT JSON_OBJECTAGG(k, v) FROM t\", read=\"mysql\", write=\"postgres\")\ntranspile(\"SELECT JSON_OBJECTAGG(KEY k VALUE v) FROM t\", read=\"oracle\", write=\"postgres\")\n# all three: ['SELECT JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v) FROM t']\n# expected:  ['SELECT JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k, v) FROM t']\n\ntranspile(\"SELECT JSON_OBJECTAGG(k VALUE v ABSENT ON NULL) FROM t\", read=\"postgres\", write=\"postgres\")\n# ['SELECT JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v, ABSENT ON NULL) FROM t']\n```\n\nOn Postgres 17, `FROM (VALUES ('a', 1), ('b', NULL)) t(k, v)`:\n- `JSON_OBJECTAGG(k VALUE v)` and `JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k, v)` both return `{ \"a\" : 1, \"b\" : null }`.\n- `JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v)` fails with `syntax error at or near \":\"`.\n- `JSON_OBJECTAGG(k: v ABSENT ON NULL)` returns `{ \"a\" : 1 }`.\n\nThe Postgres generator maps `exp.JSONObjectAgg` with `rename_func(\"JSON_OBJECT_AGG\")`, which keeps the `JSONKeyValue` as `k: v`.\n\nDocs: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-aggregate.html (`json_object_agg`, `json_objectagg`)\n\n## Discussion (before PR)\n\n@hector2394:\nI reproduced `JSON_OBJECT_AGG(k: v)` locally with the PostgreSQL, MySQL, and Oracle inputs from the report. #9250 adds regression tests for all three inputs and `ABSENT ON NULL`.",
